``(4) Practical end-use products.--Technologies selected for demonstration at the pilot scale shall be intended to result in practical end-use products.
``(5) Assistance by the secretary.--The Secretary shall assist the project to ensure expeditious completion by providing sufficient quantities of contaminated dredged material to conduct the full-scale demonstrations to stated capacity.'';

Section 219(e) of the Water Resources Development Act of 1992 (106 Stat. 4835; 110 Stat. 3757) is amended by striking paragraphs (5) and (6) and inserting the following:
``(5) $25,000,000 for the project described in subsection (c)(2);
``(6) $20,000,000 for the project described in subsection (c)(9);
``(7) $30,000,000 for the project described in subsection (c)(16); and
``(8) $30,000,000 for the project described in subsection (c)(17).''.

Section 1103(e) of the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (33 U.S.C. 652(e)) is amended by striking paragraph (2) and inserting the following:
``(2) Reports.--Not later than December 31, 2004, and not later than December 31 of every sixth year thereafter, the Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of the Interior and the States of Illinois, Iowa, Minnesota, Missouri, and Wisconsin, shall submit to Congress a report that--
``(A) contains an evaluation of the programs described in paragraph (1);
``(B) describes the accomplishments of each of the programs;
``(C) provides updates of a systemic habitat needs assessment; and
``(D) identifies any needed adjustments in the authorization of the programs.''.
